1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>1/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>A projectile has ordinary range d when launched at speed v and angle theta under gravity g. At the highest point it enters a region where the effective downward acceleration is g/0.81. If its new total horizontal range is d&#x27;=n d, find n.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>The acceleration changes only after the projectile reaches its apex.</li><li>Horizontal velocity is unchanged at the boundary.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Recomputing the whole flight with the modified gravity instead of changing only the descent.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9