-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Write the ball-minus-stone relative position; what happens to the identical gravitational acceleration terms?</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Use the vertical collision condition to eliminate the stone&#x27;s unknown launch speed.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Evaluate the resulting collision-time expression for the two angle pairs.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="#g9-CORE1A--MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="#g9-CORE1A--MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Because both bodies have the same gravitational acceleration, subtracting their position equations removes the -gt^2/2 term.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>For collision, the vertical relative displacement condition gives the stone speed in terms of v0 and the two angles; eliminating it yields T = L sin(theta1)/[v0 sin(theta0+theta1)].</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Thus T1=L/(sqrt(2)v0) and T2=L/(2v0), so (T1/T2)^2=2.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> 2.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>2.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>Both angle pairs have theta0+theta1=90°, so only <span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>\u2061</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sin (theta1)</annotation></semantics></math></span> changes: <span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>\u2061</mo><mn>45</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sin 45</annotation></semantics></math></span>/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>\u2061</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sin 30</annotation></semantics></math></span>=sqrt2.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="g9-CORE2--PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences Medium concept Multi-step reasoning Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Single-correct multiple choice IIT-JEE 2012 · Paper I · Q5 Verified past-exam adaptation A block on a frictionless horizontal surface is attached to a spring of natural length 4.9 m whose other end is fixed to a wall. It is stretched by 0.2 m and released, executing SHM with angular frequency pi/3 rad/s. At the same instant a pebble is launched at 45 degrees, toward the block, from a point on the surface 10 m from the wall (on the block&#x27;s side). If it meets the block after 1 s, determine the launch speed. Take g=10 m/s^2. The spring-block motion and projectile launch begin simultaneously. The block starts from maximum extension. Distances along the surface are measured from the wall to which the spring is fixed; the block starts 5.1 m from it and the pebble&#x27;s launch point is 10 m from it. (A) sqrt(50) m/s (B) sqrt(51) m/s (C) sqrt(52) m/s (D) sqrt(53) m/s" class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>IIT-JEE · 2012 · Paper I · Q5</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-KIN-2D-MOTION" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2 D"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2 D</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05" data-g9-meta-value="D3"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Multi-step reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-KIN-2D-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2D component and projectile practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2D component and projectile practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05" data-g9-meta-value="single_correct_mcq"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Single-correct multiple choice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05" data-g9-meta-value="IIT-JEE 2012 · Paper I · Q5"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>IIT-JEE 2012 · Paper I · Q5</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/past_qps/2012_1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D3">D3 · 7/10 · about 3 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Synchronizes an SHM event with a projectile event using one shared time.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>1/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>A block on a frictionless horizontal surface is attached to a spring of natural length 4.9 m whose other end is fixed to a wall. It is stretched by 0.2 m and released, executing SHM with angular frequency pi/3 rad/s. At the same instant a pebble is launched at 45 degrees, toward the block, from a point on the surface 10 m from the wall (on the block&#x27;s side). If it meets the block after 1 s, determine the launch speed.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>Take g=10 m/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</li><li>The spring-block motion and projectile launch begin simultaneously.</li><li>The block starts from maximum extension.</li><li>Distances along the surface are measured from the wall to which the spring is fixed; the block starts 5.1 m from it and the pebble&#x27;s launch point is 10 m from it.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Solving the projectile without first locating the moving block at t=1 s.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="3"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Evaluate the spring extension at t=1 s from its cosine law.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Translate the resulting block position into the pebble&#x27;s required horizontal displacement.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Check the vertical projectile displacement at the same time.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="#g9-CORE1A--MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="#g9-CORE1A--MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>After 1 s the spring extension is 0.2 cos(pi/3) = 0.1 m, so the block is 4.9 + 0.1 = 5.0 m from the wall.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>The pebble starts 10 m from the wall and must reach the block, 5.0 m from the wall, in 1 s: it covers 5 m horizontally, so v cos45 = 5.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2012-P1-Q05-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Hence v=5sqrt(2)=sqrt(50) m/s; its vertical displacement after 1 s is also zero, so the meeting height is consistent.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> Option (A): sqrt(50) m/s.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>Option (A): <span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mn>50</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{50}</annotation></semantics></math></span> m/s.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>With v/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>=5 m/s, y(1)=5-5=0 and the horizontal coordinate is exactly the block coordinate.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="g9-CORE2--PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences Medium concept Multi-step reasoning Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Numerical value JEE (Advanced) 2022 · Paper 1 · Q8 Verified past-exam adaptation A projectile has ordinary range d when launched at speed v and angle theta under gravity g. At the highest point it enters a region where the effective downward acceleration is g/0.81. If its new total horizontal range is d&#x27;=n d, find n. The acceleration changes only after the projectile reaches its apex. Horizontal velocity is unchanged at the boundary." class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE (Advanced) · 2022 · Paper 1 · Q8</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><stron